# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The package provides two ways to look at a shaded lightcone:\n"
msgstr "El paquete ofrece dos formas de ver un shaded lightcone:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`draw_shaded_lightcone` overlays the bounds onto the circuit diagram. THis is best for circuits on a 1D\n"
"chain of qubits, where the circuit diagram and the physical layout agree.\n"
msgstr ""
"`draw_shaded_lightcone` superpone las cotas al diagrama del circuito. Es lo mejor para circuitos sobre una cadena 1D\n"
"de qubits, donde el diagrama del circuito y la disposición física coinciden.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` projects the bounds onto the QPU's coupling map and steps through the\n"
"circuit layer by layer. This is best when the qubit connectivity is more than a 1D line, where a circuit\n"
"diagram stops conveying which qubits are neighbors.\n"
msgstr ""
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` proyecta las cotas sobre el mapa de acoplamiento de la QPU y recorre el\n"
"circuito capa por capa. Es lo mejor cuando la conectividad de los qubits es más que una línea 1D, donde un diagrama\n"
"de circuito deja de transmitir qué qubits son vecinos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both visualizations show the same underlying numbers. This guide covers what those numbers mean, and explains the details\n"
"that are easy to misread.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ambas visualizaciones muestran los mismos números subyacentes. Esta guía explica qué significan esos números y detalla\n"
"los aspectos que son fáciles de malinterpretar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Configuración {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the same Trotterized Ising circuit and observable as the [quickstart guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart).\n"
msgstr "Usa el mismo circuito de Ising con Trotter y el mismo observable que la [guía de inicio rápido](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "`draw_shaded_lightcone` {#draw_shaded_lightcone}"
msgstr "`draw_shaded_lightcone` {#draw_shaded_lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each noisy box is shaded by the bound on the errors occurring there: bright means a large bound, and\n"
"a box fading into the background means its errors have little effect on the observable. Those faded\n"
"boxes are the candidates for dropping from the mitigated noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cada box ruidoso se sombrea según la cota de los errores que ocurren en él: brillante significa una cota grande, y\n"
"un box que se desvanece en el fondo significa que sus errores tienen poco efecto en el observable. Esos boxes\n"
"desvanecidos son los candidatos para eliminarse del modelo de ruido mitigado.\n"

